            "text": "{\n  \"units\": [\n    {\n      \"quote_ref\": \"F000\",\n      \"scope_refs\": [],\n      \"kind\": \"requirement\",\n      \"meaning\": \"If an employer does not maintain an accurate record of hours worked by an employee—including employees who are exempt from the FLSA requirement that a record be kept of their hours worked (such as bona fide executive, administrative, and professional employees as defined in 29 CFR part 541)—the employer bears the burden of showing that the employee has not worked the requisite hours of service.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"quote_ref\": \"F000\",\n      \"scope_refs\": [],\n      \"kind\": \"requirement\",\n      \"meaning\": \"As an example under the rule placing the burden of proof on employers who do not maintain accurate hours records, an employer must be able to clearly demonstrate that full-time teachers (defined in § 825.102) of an elementary or secondary school system, institution of higher education, or other educational establishment or institution (who often work outside the classroom or at their homes) did not work 1,250 hours during the previous 12 months in order to claim that the teachers are not eligible for FMLA leave.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"quote_ref\": \"F000\",\n      \"scope_refs\": [],\n      \"kind\": \"background\",\n      \"meaning\": \"The statement directing readers to § 825.801(d) for special rules applicable to airline flight crew employees is an administrative cross-reference that establishes no independent substantive rule within this passage.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
